Two translation bugs in the crit-bit comparison logic, both the same mistake:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
1. [1m[38;5;10mblt_setp[0m (line ~215)[22m — The insertion point comparison had swapped operands. The C code compares [38;5;10m(new_byte << 8) + existing_node_mask[0m against [38;5;10m(existing_byte << 8) + new_mask[0m, but the Rust translation compared [38;5;10m(new_byte << 8) + new_mask[0m against [38;5;10m(existing_byte << 8) + existing_mask[0m. This caused keys to be inserted at wrong positions in the tree, breaking sorted order.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
2. [1m[38;5;10mblt_ceilfloor[0m (line ~500)[22m — Same swapped comparison, causing ceil/floor lookups to walk the tree incorrectly.[0m[0m
